re consumption  better in the cloud  the answer is we offer a fully  compatible vmware experience  so you can bring your existing tools and  processes  as is you can bring vmware first party  tools  for operations management for dr  for large-scale infrastructure  management through vrealize automation  and bcloud director you can also take  advantage of the vmware ecosystem  of a providers technology providers  in the spaces of backup business  continuity dr  monitoring security  networking and so forth in addition you  can take advantage of google cloud  services  which can improve the way you monitor  vmware  as well as the rest of your applications  the way you backup the way you do  application development the way you can  do  warehousing and i'm going to give very  concrete and specific examples of all of  these in subsequent slides  in addition third parties are building  support for google cloud  uh netapp is an uh partner that offers  native support for their storage  platform  uh which is integrated with google cloud  and  and it enables use cases such as br  data movement and also workload storage  so i've talked about some examples now  let's double click  into how google cloud can actually  supercharge vmware consumption  by looking at some examples of service  integrations  so once you have your vmware environment  up and running in google cloud  a key question is how do you enable data  protection for  production workloads backup  is the most common way to achieve that  the good news is that since the service  offers a native vmware platform  it is fully compatible with your  existing vmware based  backup tools so you can get into  production quickly with  no change however in the cloud you can  do better  in your on-premise deployments you often  have secondary storage  which are lower cost storage  environments to store backups  however to ensure that you can survive  local site failures you often have to do  off-site backups  into tape drives through tape drives or  perhaps into the cloud  but now that your vmware is literally in  the cloud  there is no need to make expensive  copies and to ship data to multiple  locations to get better  availability and disaster resiliency  you can back up your data into cloud  storage and choose how quickly you want  to restore  your data as well as the redundancy  level  of your storage backups  so for example you can choose to have  your data stored in near line storage  and select geo redundancy to ensure that  you can survive  a single site failure at an extremely  low price point  thus you can get better recovery times  better availability  and at much lower cost compared to your  on-premise  backup infrastructure  now your vmware infrastructure has  production workloads  databases and line of business  applications  as you look to modernize this  infrastructure you want to take  advantage of technologies like  containers and kubernetes well  anthos lets you build and manage  container-based hybrid and multi-cloud  applications  you develop once and run these  applications  across your existing on-premises  infrastructure  or any major public cloud provider  using anthos you can run these  applications on vmware engine  as well some of these benefits  some of the benefits of doing this is  that you get a dedicated  private environment with latest hardware  100 gigs of networking your workloads  can be right  next to the databases for the lowest  latency and best performance  and since your environment is single  tenant you get the benefits of the  privacy and the security of dedicated  infra  now as you consume vmware in the cloud  you also want to ensure  that you avoid the screen swivel for  operations management  for example if you have a performance  problem you want to troubleshoot  all aspects of the application  dependencies in one place  rather than go to different systems to  solve different parts of the problem  while the vmware engine fully supports  existing vmware monitoring and logging  tools without changes  as you start to develop hybrid  applications for example using anthos  that partially might live outside of  vmware  getting all of your operations data in  one place is going to be important  to solve this problem you can use google  cloud's operations  formerly it was known as stackdriver  to collect metrics logs traces  across vmware engine as well as other  google cloud services  you can then use the built-in out of the  box dashboards to view and monitor the  platform and the applications  and you can then query and analyze these  signals intelligently  and you can see information from the  platform  from vcenter from esxi and you can do  log analysis  there's no agent required and in fact vm  level data  cpu memory disk and network usage  are all included all available as part  of the signals that come from the vmware  platform without having to install any  agents inside the workloads themselves  the vms themselves  but if you so want you want deeper view  into the application metrics  telemetry then you can use open source  agents  and collect additional logs and metrics  from inside the vm  and from the application context  directly  so if you want to troubleshoot any  application or gain insights for  optimization or usage  you can do it all in one place in  google cloud's operations  now when you peek inside a typical  vmware deployment  you're going to find that the top  workloads are often based on databases  like  sql server and oracle  and typically these are operational  transactional databases  that feed into data warehousing  infrastructures  often these warehousing infrastructures  are proprietary  and expensive they require explicit  infrastructure management and  maintenance  but google provides data services that  simplifies  and supercharges these this process  bigquery is a serverless highly scalable  and cost effective data warehouse  designed to help you turn  big data into informed business  decisions  it works seamlessly for real-time  analytics  and automatically scales  as your data scales so that your data  continues to make sense to you without  you having to  change your infrastructure every time  you have a scale change  tools like tableau and data studio work  seamlessly with bigquery to help you  better understand your information  and you can use services such as cloud  data flow  to incrementally ingest data embellish  it  with different sources coming from  various different systems  clean it dynamically before it's fed  into the big query system  so you can become more efficient  more intelligent and more agile with  data analytic with data analysis  and save cost while you are at it  so as you can see the service enables  you to not only bring  vmware to google cloud but  also the services and innovation of  google cloud to vmware to give you the  best of both worlds  so now that you've seen all the features  and benefits of running vmware in google  cloud  when and where can you get it  as you see the deployment plan in this  screen  google cloud is fully committed to make  sure that  you get vmware in the location you  prefer  we are expanding quickly and widely  and you should be able to consume vmware  in 10 regions by the end of this year  and i have to note that this is the  fastest  and widest deployment of a vmware  in the public cloud from any provider  so to summarize you can see that google  has a number of  technical advantage that gives you a  very compelling  very compatible and high performance  enterprise infrastructure  for your vmware environments  the vmware service that vmware engine  offers  is fully integrated with google cloud  it gives you the highest level of  availability of  any cloud provider and you get a single  source  for all your vmware and cloud needs  including support transaction billing  and so forth so it's a very cost  effective  and very compelling offer  that helps you supercharge your cloud  transformation  and application modernization  so that's a wrap folks if you would like  to find out more  you can go to the product page at  cloud.google.com  vmware engine if you have any questions  for the product team you can send an  email to vmware  engine google.com and you can also  check out other sessions chat with  vmware engine experts  and also check out a digital demo via  the next  on air page with that  i thank you for your time and attention  today  and i hope you all stay safe  thank you
 

